  "rationale": "**The matcher and the CLI paths are correct, but the requirement's other two selection sites lack `{impl}` markers and have no direct tests.**\n\nWhat is correct:\n- `src/definition_glob.rs` `validate` rejects an empty glob and any character other than alphanumerics, `.`, `_`, `-` and `*`.\n- `matches` is a whole-name dynamic-programming matcher. `*` matches zero or more characters, including dots, and every other byte matches literally.\n- `status_markdown_with_options` and `info_markdown` in `src/commands.rs` validate the glob, skip terms, and filter with `matches`. Both return an error when nothing matches.\n- Unit and CLI tests cover:\n  - wildcards crossing dots;\n  - whole-name anchoring;\n  - an empty or invalid glob;\n  - an invalid `[` glob in `info` and `status`;\n  - `requirements.*ready` matching two requirements;\n  - an unmatched glob.\n\nThe requirement says every definition selection MUST use this rule, \"including requirements evidence inputs, CLI definition filters, and the authoring `references` tool\". Several code paths implement that rule without an `{impl}` reference to it:\n- **Requirements evidence input:** `src/inputs.rs` `resolve`, in the `Requirements` branch, calls `definition_glob::validate` and `matches`. Its markers cover only `requirements.definitions.inputs` and `requirements.definitions.selection`.\n- **Authoring `references` tool:** `src/authoring/tools.rs` `references` calls `validate` and `matches`. Its only marker is `requirements.authoring.reference_index`.\n- **Authoring input access:** `src/authoring/inputs.rs` `source_input` also calls `matches` on the requirements selector. It has no marker for this requirement either.\n- **Status wrapper:** `status_markdown_filtered` in `src/commands.rs` is marked only with `requirements.definitions.selection`.\n\nTest coverage is also thin for two of the three named surfaces. No `{test}` reference to this requirement exercises glob selection through the `requirements` evidence input form (`src/inputs.rs`) or through the authoring `references` tool, including their empty and invalid glob behaviour. The unit tests and the CLI tests cover only the matcher and the `status` and `info` commands.\n\nI found no FIXME acknowledging these gaps.",
